  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The proposed extensions, including rear dormer and roof lights and, in particular, the hip to gable conversion on this prominent corner plot, by reason of their excessive size, bulk and appearance and incoherent design, would be disproportionately large in relation to the roof and constitute an obtrusive feature out of character with the established roofline of adjoining properties and the wider street scene contrary to policies ENV-B 1.1 and H 6.4 of the Adopted Unitary Development Plan and the Council's Residential Extension Guidelines.",
    "Condition : 2 - The applicant is advised that access to the frontage of the property is currently from a dropped kerb provided for pedestrian use. This is contrary to the Highways Act 1980."
